# Second brain ({{ brain_root }})

Obsidian-compatible **markdown vault**. Files are the brain; software is
replaceable. This directory is seeded by the lab-provisioning `brain` role.

## Open it

- Any editor / git
- Optional: [Obsidian](https://obsidian.md) → **Open folder as vault** → this directory
  (template folder = `templates/`)

No app or MCP from this repo is required.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `inbox/` | Raw drops; process later |
| `notes/postmortems/` | Lessons from bad answers / failed runs |
| `notes/decisions/` | Adopt/reject choices |
| `templates/` | Copy-from postmortem / decision skeletons |
| `playbooks/` | ACE tactics for agents (`qloop` / agentlab) |
| `mocs/` | Maps of content (optional) |
| `sources/` | Archived clips (optional) |
| `journal/` | Daily notes (optional) |

## Learn from mistakes

1. Copy `templates/postmortem.md` → `notes/postmortems/YYYY-MM-DD-title.md`
2. Fill symptom → bad question → TASK PACKAGE gaps → fix
3. Promote durable rules into `playbooks/*.md` or:
   `qloop playbook reflect playbooks/infra.md --task "…" --trace "…" --outcome "FAIL …"`

## Governance

- Personal/lab vault by default — no client-confidential dumps without isolation
- Agents may draft; humans accept before treating notes as ground truth
- Backed up when `enable_backups` includes this path

